WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.700
<b>Oden's Adventure</b>

3
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.610
It's my dream
to explore the world!

4
00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.570
Sailing far and wide!

5
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.540
Take me with you!

6
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.000
We should leave
promptly!

7
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.130
– You really think we'd go for that?
– You really think we'd go for that?

8
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.920
Ugh, that's enough out of you!

9
00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.800
I've been held back
for far too long!

10
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.140
I want to escape this
suffocating island!

11
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.560
Please!
Free me from these chains!

12
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.390
Lord Oden, no! Stop that!
Raise your head!

13
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.640
I'm sorry.

14
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.650
Weren't you just trying
to kill our captain?

15
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.110
I beg you!

16
00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.400
Enough! This man
is a pirate, not an ally!

17
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.570
You're a scourge!

18
00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.450
Leave this country
before it's too late!

19
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.830
Well. I would leave if I could.

20
00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.330
But as you can see, our ship
was damaged on the way here,

21
00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.660
so that presents
a slight problem.

22
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.210
That won't do at all!

23
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.630
I'll help you repair it!

24
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.670
Listen well!

25
00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.590
I cannot have you tempting
Lord Oden like this!

26
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.130
Repair the ship quickly and go!

27
00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.720
That's exactly my intention.

28
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.190
Stop dragging your feet!

29
00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.770
Bring it here!

30
00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.320
Hey! You ready
for a snack break?

31
00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.610
We've got some grub for ya!

32
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.240
Dig in! No need to be shy!

33
00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.740
That looks good!

34
00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.630
The flavor of
a far off land!

35
00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.500
And what, pray tell, is this?

36
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.670
It's alcohol made from grapes.

37
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.550
So many things out there
I need to see.

38
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.720
Show me more!

39
00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.300
Take me with you!

40
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.390
I wanna solve every
mystery in the world!

41
00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.810
You're not the type
to serve under someone.

42
00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.860
I can see it already.

43
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.520
I can't let just
anyone on my ship.

44
00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.150
Do you know what
happens when there are

45
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.150
too many selfish people around?

46
00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:40.870
People like you, I mean?

47
00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.660
It's too hot!

48
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.250
It's not pretty.

49
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.040
I learned that the hard way
with the last ship I was on.

50
00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.430
Why not
set sail on your own?

51
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.970
I've tried over and over again!

52
00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.680
But every damn time,
it ends in failure!

53
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.480
I may be strong,
but that doesn't mean

54
00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.180
I can navigate a ship!

55
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.730
Then give up on sailing
and do whatever your job is!

56
00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.400
This country is
suffocating me, all right?

57
00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.570
I need to be free!

58
00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.240
Listen, Whitebeard!

59
00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.530
The Land of Wano has a law that

60
00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.200
strictly bars people
from leaving here.

61
00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.870
Lord Oden is now
the Daimyo of Kuri,

62
00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.120
so it would be inexcusable
for him to break that law!

63
00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.920
Don't tell him about that!

64
00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.080
Well, good to know!

65
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.250
Seems you and I are
on the same page.

66
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.160
I don't want your "Daimyo"
on my ship, either!

67
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.580
Do you think I care about
some stuffy old laws?

68
00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.760
How insightful of you!

69
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.220
Yes! Lord Oden is
indispensable to our land!

70
00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.720
That's enough! You'll be fine!

71
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.310
Take me to sea,
Whitebeard! Please!

72
00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.900
Help me! I don't wanna
be the daimyo! No!

73
00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.440
Please, don't make me go home!

74
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.440
This place is suffocating,
I tell you!

75
00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.780
Untie me, you beasts! How cruel!

76
00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.540
I won't give up!

77
00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.120
You cannot stop me!

78
00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:25.300
Whitebeard! Wait for me!

79
00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.320
You think there's only
five islands in the world?

80
00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:33.540
Not even close!

81
00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.040
– What?!
– What?!

82
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.000
Try 10 million!
Maybe even 20 million. Or more!

83
00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.960
Jeez! You guys
don't know anything!

84
00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.010
Sailing the world is a blast!

85
00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.550
You should try it!

86
00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.660
The world out there
is a big place!

87
00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.870
There's so many islands,

88
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.200
you could never
hope to see them all!

89
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.090
<b>Two Weeks Later</b>

90
00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.120
Sneaking off?

91
00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.530
Where might you be going?
It's quite late.

92
00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.330
You frightened me half to death!

93
00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.700
Where are you going?

94
00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.290
Does the daimyo need your
permission to take a piss?

95
00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.630
Give me a break! It's nothing!

96
00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.130
Do take care, Lord Oden.
The night can be cold.

97
00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:29.100
Ridiculous!

98
00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.600
Oden won't be happy

99
00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:37.140
we snuck away
at night like this.

100
00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.560
A pity, since he was so strong.

101
00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.150
He might've been
an asset to the crew.

102
00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.190
It really seemed like
Pops liked him, too.

103
00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.990
I thought he'd say yes.

104
00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.160
Huh? What're you talking about?

105
00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.990
Don't play dumb with us!

106
00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.170
Hypothetically, even if I did
take a liking to him,

107
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.460
we still couldn't bring him
along with us.

108
00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.420
That would be like
kidnapping royalty.

109
00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.550
Did you leave him that
treasure chest like I told you?

110
00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.100
We owe them for all the food
and supplies they gave us.

111
00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:19.950
Hm? What the hell is that?

112
00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:20.310
You pirates thought you could

113
00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.280
You pirates thought you
could pull one over on me, huh?

114
00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.450
pull one over on me, huh?

115
00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:25.280
Well, too bad!

116
00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:26.950
Ah! Oden.

117
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:27.200
Oden!

118
00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.240
Now let me on that ship!

119
00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.120
Not so fast!

120
00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:31.210
I know you think
you're clever, my lord,

121
00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.780
I know you think you're
clever, my lord,

122
00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:32.830
but you're not
getting away that easily!

123
00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.540
but you're not getting
away that easily!

124
00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.120
Now come with me!

125
00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.580
That idiot!

126
00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.250
Show me the world!

127
00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.500
Take me with you! Whitebeard!

128
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.090
We need you here!

129
00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:48.590
You're to be the next shogun!

130
00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.420
Sorry, pal, no means no.

131
00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.470
But good luck
ruling or whatever!

132
00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.930
I'm letting you loose now!

133
00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.140
Wait just a moment.

134
00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.060
I'm concerned about the man
who's chasing after Oden.

135
00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.730
Bring him up here.

136
00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.820
What a pain.

137
00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:07.440
Now, everyone hold on!

138
00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.400
Don't worry about
those morons from Wano!

139
00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:14.200
We're about to fly
over those falls!

140
00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:21.370
Oh no, oh no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no!

141
00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:31.820
<b>Wano</b>

142
00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:38.730
Izo's gone, too!
Even the doggie and kitty!

143
00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.520
Don't cry, Okiku!

144
00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.020
Instead of fearing the worst,
we should search for them!

145
00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:43.070
As a team! You with me?

146
00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.320
As a team!

147
00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.700
You with me?

148
00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:50.780
Start the search!
Cover the whole country!

149
00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.380
Hey! He's had enough!

150
00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.340
You can't let Lord Oden die!

151
00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.090
Pull up the chain!

152
00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:04.430
We need him!

153
00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:07.600
The future of our country
rests on his shoulders!

154
00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:08.760
Listen, kid,

155
00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.810
you saw me tell him no
again and again.

156
00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:15.230
He's the one who turned his back
on that country of yours.

157
00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:19.900
We're on my ship, and that means
we're gonna play by my rules.

158
00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.950
Don't do this! I'm begging you!

159
00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.160
That man is dangerous.

160
00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.620
I can't let him
force his way on board.

161
00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.370
I have to protect
my family first.

162
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.250
If you want to stop him,
talk him down yourself.

163
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:43.420
Listen up, Oden! Three days!

164
00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:46.430
You hang on to that chain
for three days,

165
00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.640
then I'll let you come aboard.

166
00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:54.940
Do you swear it? On your life?

167
00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.400
Yeah! You have my word!

168
00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.820
I can't tell,
is Oden still there?

169
00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:41.030
Uh... Yeah, he is.

170
00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.740
But he's looking,
uh... not great.

171
00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.030
Between the waves
and everything else

172
00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:49.080
crashing into his face,
he's pretty busted up.

173
00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.540
Only one hour left, Oden!

174
00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.460
You got this! Let's go!

175
00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.000
Hey! You shouldn't be
cheering for the guy!

176
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.260
But Pops said he could
join us if he pulls this off,

177
00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.090
don't you get it?

178
00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.760
He's gonna become
a member of our crew!

179
00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.720
Oden...
will be our new crewmate?

180
00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.900
You can do it! Just hang on!

181
00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.030
Oden! Yeah, attaboy!

182
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.740
You can't give up now! C'mon!

183
00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:37.360
fools.

184
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.630
I don't care if it's your ship,

185
00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.420
no one treats my lord like this
and gets away with it!

186
00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.340
I'll make you pay!

187
00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:51.140
Keep it up, Oden! C'mon!

188
00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.560
Hang on!

189
00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.360
Lord Oden, no!

190
00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:03.400
No! Take your hands off of me!

191
00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.750
<b>Amatsuki Toki</b>

192
00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:17.880
What a babe!
And she's so classy!

193
00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:22.680
<b>A Certain Nearby Island</b>

194
00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.420
Why are you running?

195
00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.590
We'll take you to Wano
just like you asked!

196
00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.420
We've got a nice, big ship
waiting for you!

197
00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.380
You don't have to be scared!

198
00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.300
We won't hurt you!

199
00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:30.720
I know you won't.

200
00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.430
Your vessel is
a slave ship after all.

201
00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:36.640
If you hurt me,
I'll be worth less.

202
00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:40.360
I should've fled the moment
I saw your wicked-looking faces.

203
00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.190
How foolish of me.

204
00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.610
You're gonna drown, girl!

205
00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:48.570
There's nowhere left to run!

206
00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.030
Just give up!

207
00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:52.780
You're wrong.
I can still escape.

208
00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:54.740
Put that big sword away.

209
00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:57.370
I promise we'll treat you nice!

210
00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:01.210
You'll be our little
treasure, okay?

211
00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.420
It's time. I must escape
into the future once again.

212
00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.730
hurt you?

213
00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.690
What? No, I'm just
a little shaken up.

214
00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:19.660
But wait, does that mean
you came here to save me?

215
00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:23.280
I did.

216
00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:28.710
I'm so glad you're all right.

217
00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.010
You're in much worse
shape than me!

218
00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:40.720
Come on! Stay with me, please!

219
00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.120
Oden disappeared!

220
00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.790
What happened, where did he go?

221
00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:52.460
Damn it! There were only
a few minutes left to go!

222
00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.630
He was so close to making it,
but he couldn't hold on.

223
00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.000
He's dead!

224
00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.340
I don't think it's fair
what you did to him, Pops!

225
00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.470
Yeah, he gave it
his best back there!

226
00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.430
You should've let him join us!

227
00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:07.100
Lord Oden! Lord Oden!

228
00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:08.510
Hey, stop it!

229
00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:29.480
He's recovering so fast!

230
00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:32.230
I didn't realize he was a human.

231
00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.630
<b>The Next Day</b>

232
00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:52.810
Wow. A fierce struggle,

233
00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.980
but I still couldn't
get on Whitebeard's ship!

234
00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:57.110
All those dreams of
touring around the world

235
00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:00.860
just sailed right away!
But no matter!

236
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.870
I still did it!

237
00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:13.170
I set foot on foreign soil for
the first time ever! Finally!

238
00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.880
So cheery!

239
00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.050
My adventure has begun at last!

240
00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:21.300
The Land of Wano
is far behind me now!

241
00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.930
The world is
my oyster! I'm free!

242
00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.970
Don't jump around so much!

243
00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:30.270
You're healing fast, but you're
not fully recovered yet!

244
00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:31.980
Huh?

245
00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:35.400
I see! So you're the woman
who nursed me back to health?

246
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.400
Yes? Sort of.

247
00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.020
Thank you very much!

248
00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:40.820
Oh, no!

249
00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:43.780
It's the least I could do
after you saved me!

250
00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:45.990
Truly, I am in your debt, sir.

251
00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:49.620
Well, Miss, we're both safe now
and that's all that matters.

252
00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.500
By the way, did I
hear you say that you're

253
00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.250
from the Land of Wano?

254
00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.670
That I am, yes.

255
00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.340
And speaking of which.

256
00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.130
I've come all the way
to a foreign land,

257
00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.760
but you're dressed like you're
from the Flower Capital!

258
00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:05.220
I would have thought you'd
wear something more exotic.

259
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.350
Well, the truth is,
since I was a child,

260
00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.970
it's been my dream to
visit the Land of Wano!

261
00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.440
When you return home,

262
00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:18.770
would you be so kind as to
take me along with you?

263
00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.110
Um...

264
00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:22.320
Uh...

265
00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:23.900
He's annoyed...

266
00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.870
That's her! Right over there!

267
00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:37.330
We're
counting on you, Captain Karma!

268
00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:41.370
<b>Captain Karma
Cephaloctopus Pirates</b>

269
00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:46.090
Six arms? Wow! Fascinating!

270
00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:48.800
Back at home, we don't have
anybody built like that!

271
00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.930
Huh? Hey. I thought
you guys said there was

272
00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.810
a monster protecting her.

273
00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:58.440
Huh? That's funny.
Where'd it go?

274
00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:03.320
I mean, it's way
too big to hide.

275
00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:06.660
Well! You're back!
Can't get enough?

276
00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.030
And who are you?

277
00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:10.740
Don't act like
you know us, bastard!

278
00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:14.870
Huh? Did all of you hit
your heads or something?

279
00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.460
Shoulda known a high-class lady

280
00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:18.500
would've had
a bodyguard with her.

281
00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.540
But it'll be worth
the price she fetches!

282
00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.130
I'll kick your ass
and then sell you both!

283
00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:29.680
Let's run away.
There are too many of them!

284
00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:33.760
My first fight overseas,
I can't wait!

285
00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.270
Pirates!

286
00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:53.370
This man,
Karma, eventually became

287
00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.450
an associate of
the Whitebeard Pirates,

288
00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:59.670
and even fought beside them
during the war in Marineford.

289
00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.130
Come aboard. Let's go.

290
00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.880
Huh? But I let go of
the chain back there.

291
00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.880
What made you change your mind?

292
00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:11.340
One woman screams
and you throw your dream away?

293
00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:13.840
Heh. Quite the softie,
aren't you?

294
00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.680
Hurry. Before I change my mind.

295
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:21.220
We're setting out
on an amazing adventure.

296
00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.810
We're setting out
on an amazing adventure,

297
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:26.020
One beyond your wildest dreams!

298
00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:23.810
one beyond your wildest dreams!

299
00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.400
Ready, little brother?

300
00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.520
Are you sure, White-kichi?

301
00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.070
Hm? Are you talking to me?

302
00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.200
Let's set sail!

303
00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.960
Oden!

304
00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.590
We're so glad you're alive!

305
00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:56.340
I was starting to think
we lost you to the sea!

306
00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.260
Yeah, what a relief!

307
00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:04.560
Glad to be here!
Thank you!

308
00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.890
Pops gave you
a rough time back there, huh?

309
00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.600
Real nasty stuff!

310
00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.190
What a jerk, huh?

311
00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.400
Hey! I heard that!

312
00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.400
Y-You're alive!

313
00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.990
It's such a relief
to see you safe! Sir!

314
00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.450
Yes! And better
than ever, my friend!

315
00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.620
We're here, too!

316
00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.840
D-Dogstorm? Cat Viper?

317
00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:33.670
Where the hell
did you come from?

318
00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.960
We figured you-gara would get
on the ship one way or another,

319
00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.630
so we snuck on and
hid before it left Wano.

320
00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.890
Wherever you-gara go,
we'll follow!

321
00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:47.590
A while back, you said you were
gonna make me pay, didn't you?

322
00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:52.260
If you want to throw me
into the sea, then do it!

323
00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.710
What?

324
00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:03.730
Maybe I will someday!

325
00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.190
Miss! What's your name?

326
00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:09.360
Oh! Pleasure to
meet you, I'm Toki.

327
00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.570
Thank you so much
for helping me.

328
00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.740
So, um... If it's not a bother,

329
00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.830
could you take me to
the Land of Wano?

330
00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:19.480
He's annoyed!

331
00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:22.610
I'll help out however I can,

332
00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:25.280
so please let me
stay on board this ship!

333
00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:26.660
Do as you like!

334
00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.710
Every sight, every sound,
and every experience that I have

335
00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:40.130
will be faithfully
chronicled in my journal.

336
00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:48.140
Enemy ship! Prepare
for battle, everyone!

337
00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.180
Here we go!

338
00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:55.480
Hey! No!

339
00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:58.060
Wait!

340
00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:11.220
There! You see!

341
00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:14.040
I sank it!

342
00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:16.210
Idiot! That wasn't the plan!

343
00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:18.750
You don't get how pirates
work at all, do you?

344
00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:22.650
Plunder! You gotta
plunder the ship first!

345
00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:26.060
So many things
I've never experienced before.

346
00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.740
What is this place?

347
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.660
Tall buildings of curious make.

348
00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:36.540
Bubble-encased trees,
undulating like jelly.

349
00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:40.620
Oden! Wait!

350
00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:42.000
We dunno if it's safe!

351
00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:48.000
A world of wonders.

352
00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:54.840
No way.

353
00:22:57.010 --> 00:22:58.760
– Oden!
– Oden!

354
00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:02.890
A chill like none other.

355
00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:17.950
A heat like none other.

356
00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.330
– Oden!
– Oden!

357
00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.540
Hang on, I gotcha!

358
00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:38.560
Adventure, here I come!

359
00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:40.140
Peculiar plants.

360
00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:46.440
Oh! Hey! Come here!

361
00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:48.730
Astonishing animals.

362
00:23:51.150 --> 00:23:53.360
Humongous humans.

363
00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:56.070
Whoa!

364
00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.120
Step back, kid.

365
00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:09.170
All right!

366
00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:20.640
Strength like I've
never seen, and courage!

367
00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.640
But more than that, ideas.

368
00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:28.690
Every day, my eyes are
opened in new ways,

369
00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:30.860
and I realize how narrow
my vision was

370
00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:33.020
before I embarked
on this journey.

371
00:24:33.020 --> 00:24:37.950
I see now that I am only a tiny
piece of a great, wide world.

372
00:24:40.780 --> 00:24:43.260
How old am I? I'm 26.

373
00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:44.590
But I was born long ago,

374
00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:47.510
so technically,
I'm 800 years old.

375
00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:50.220
So what you're
saying is, you're young,

376
00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:51.600
but you're old as dirt!

377
00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:58.690
It seems that even
leaping through time

378
00:24:58.690 --> 00:25:00.360
is possible.

379
00:25:00.360 --> 00:25:02.150
The world is a big place.

380
00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:05.360
I have learned
that this world consists of

381
00:25:05.360 --> 00:25:09.450
four large seas
and one long, narrow waterway.

382
00:25:09.450 --> 00:25:13.540
And apparently, the planet
itself is round like a dumpling!

383
00:25:14.080 --> 00:25:16.210
What a mysterious thing!

384
00:25:17.840 --> 00:25:20.960
What do you think?
Enjoying the voyage?

385
00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:22.170
Certainly!

386
00:25:22.170 --> 00:25:24.970
The world is amazing.
I want to see more!

387
00:25:24.970 --> 00:25:27.550
I'm glad to hear
you're having fun!

388
00:25:27.800 --> 00:25:28.810
What is that?

389
00:25:28.810 --> 00:25:31.520
A map. In these vast seas,

390
00:25:29.760 --> 00:25:34.220
<b>South Blue</b>
<b>East Blue</b>
<b>West Blue</b>
<b>North</b>

391
00:25:31.520 --> 00:25:34.310
the Land of Wano
is hardly a speck.

392
00:25:34.310 --> 00:25:37.440
So which region is
your family from, Toki?

393
00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:40.360
I'm not sure.

394
00:25:41.070 --> 00:25:42.940
All I know is that
both of my parents

395
00:25:42.940 --> 00:25:44.860
were from the Land of Wano.

396
00:25:46.410 --> 00:25:48.160
Even if that doesn't
seem like much,

397
00:25:48.160 --> 00:25:51.040
Wano is the only place
I have left to go.

398
00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:53.540
But I'm afraid
this ship won't make it there

399
00:25:53.540 --> 00:25:55.290
for quite some time.

400
00:25:55.870 --> 00:25:57.120
Huh?

401
00:25:58.420 --> 00:26:00.170
I am sorry.

402
00:26:01.420 --> 00:26:02.590
It's fine!

403
00:26:02.590 --> 00:26:05.130
I'm rather enjoying
my travels with you.

404
00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:07.840
Because when you
and I are together,

405
00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:10.260
I feel like I'm exactly
where I need to be.

406
00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:12.890
Huh? Why is that?

407
00:26:12.890 --> 00:26:15.060
Hmm, I wonder.

408
00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:16.390
How peculiar.

409
00:26:16.390 --> 00:26:17.650
A mystery!

410
00:26:22.730 --> 00:26:24.150
– Hey, guys!

411
00:26:24.150 --> 00:26:26.280
Where'd Lord Oden run off to?

412
00:26:26.280 --> 00:26:27.320
Oh! There!

413
00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:30.070
Shh! Don't bother them!

414
00:26:43.710 --> 00:26:46.590
I soon learned that
Whitebeard has an enemy.

415
00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:49.300
The Navy's here! Let's retreat!

416
00:26:50.670 --> 00:26:52.080
Why did we flee?

417
00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:54.000
They looked like
a worthy challenge!

418
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:55.800
We should have fought them!

419
00:26:55.800 --> 00:26:57.630
You don't know the Navy, huh?

420
00:26:58.360 --> 00:27:00.190
It's a big organization.

421
00:27:00.190 --> 00:27:01.860
Even if we take them down today,

422
00:27:01.860 --> 00:27:05.400
more and more ships
will come after us.

423
00:27:05.400 --> 00:27:09.120
Wow! So there's a group that
controls the entire world, huh?

424
00:27:09.490 --> 00:27:12.410
A mighty adversary, indeed!

425
00:27:12.410 --> 00:27:14.500
Yeah, wait till you've
traveled some more.

426
00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:17.420
Then you can decide
how mighty they are.

427
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.340
Your country's
still free, after all.

428
00:27:23.290 --> 00:27:27.630
<b>In Another Sea</b>

429
00:27:29.120 --> 00:27:31.450
Nothing in the paper
today, either.

430
00:27:31.450 --> 00:27:34.210
Wha? Another story
on Whitebeard?

431
00:27:34.210 --> 00:27:36.210
But we're causing trouble, too!

432
00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:38.250
Hey, I'm still reading, dummy!

433
00:27:38.250 --> 00:27:41.340
Anyway, Whitebeard has that
Wano samurai on his crew.

434
00:27:41.340 --> 00:27:44.670
Seems like that guy's doing
crazy stuff all the time!

435
00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:48.300
– Uh, hey, Captain!
– Uh, hey, Captain!

436
00:27:51.090 --> 00:27:55.020
A samurai from a
land sealed away from the world.

437
00:27:55.020 --> 00:27:55.300
Ha. Sure hope I get to
meet him someday!

438
00:27:55.300 --> 00:27:58.100
Sure hope I get to
see him someday!

439
00:27:58.490 --> 00:28:01.870
<b>Gold Roger
A Great Pirate</b>
